e path between them.\n\nIn our case, the coordinates of the endpoints of the path $C$ are $A(0,-1,1)$ and $B(2,1,0).$\n\nApplying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r & =f(2,1,0)-f(0,-1,1) \\\\  & =(2(1)^{2}+{0}^{3})-(0(-1)^{2}+{1}^{3}) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447006 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186447008 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447006 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "22c4665d-8155-5ae8-8092-57bb12f99f4d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447006 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186259854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447007 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186447006 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447007 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "293bc725-9204-5423-bbd2-c85d97ea1144" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447007 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186259852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447008 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186447009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447008 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b5208760-54e7-5464-b42f-550fe3cbde8e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447008 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186447005 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447009 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186447010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447009 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b83ca3f6-3386-5f07-be1b-40eb7acf84d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447009 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186259859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447010 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "da6e3be4-bbf8-5d1f-a071-2461ecbb29f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447010 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186172303 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186448212 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186448212 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186448212 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "18f626fd-2f98-540d-b753-edd9dc174baa" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186448213 #edb/ref 1080 "true" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186448213 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186448213 #edb/ref 1083 